2025-11-18T14:29:15Z","closed_at":"2025-11-18T14:29:15Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nv4.4.1.stable.mono.official [49a5bc7b6]\nv4.5.beta7.official [4ebf67c12]\n\nalso tested with gdscript and it crashes as well\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.1.stable.mono - Fedora Linux 42 (Adams) on Wayland - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1650 SUPER (nvidia; 575.64.05) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-4790K CPU @ 4.00GHz (8 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nGame crashes with no error message when certain rapid synthetic mouse events (via Input.ParseInputEvent) are sent while native mouse clicks occur over a visible Control.\n\nSpecifically, it is reliably reproduced when quickly clicking left and right mouse buttons in the MRP *inside* the area of the control.\n\nThe crash does not occur if the Control is invisible, and it only triggers when both synthetic and native clicks interact with the Control.\nYou can work around the crash by adding metadata to your synthetic events and doing something like ```if (!ev.HasMeta(\"virtual_mouse\")) GetViewport().SetInputAsHandled();```. \n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Make a duplicate of mouse event. Add metadata such as \"virtual_mouse\" to prevent infinite recursion.\n2. Add a control to the scene. Resize it to fill some of the screen.\n3. Rapidly click the left and right mouse buttons within the Control area.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[synethtic-click-crash-mrp-gdscript.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22061531/synethtic-click-crash-mrp-gdscript.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubuserco